Is that a rhetorical question?  It seems like you might already know
your options, but ...

You've got a few options:
- acquire divine protection,
- enchant the armor you choose to wear;
- wear body armor, max out your luck so that you still hit in melee
and ignore the spam;
- cast magic missile (compatible with armor, having the Eye of the
Aethiopica helps a lot);
- get a strong pet (compatible with armor);
- get enough HP that poor AC does not matter;
- fire a crossbow or throw darts, or shuriken for extra style points
(compatible with armor);
- walk away from hazards;

By the way, are you playing atheist conduct or just not acquiring
divine protection?  Either way is fine but there is a reason conducts
are conducts, they make the game more difficult.

